1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,336
Two identical porch lights, on all night.

2
00:00:02,456 --> 00:00:04,489
One is a sixty-watt incandescent.

3
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:06,405
The other, a nine-watt LED.

4
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:07,502
Same brightness.

5
00:00:07,622 --> 00:00:10,177
Twelve hours a night, every night of the year.

6
00:00:10,297 --> 00:00:17,627
The incandescent costs about forty-seven dollars and eighty cents a year, at the national average electricity price.

7
00:00:17,747 --> 00:00:21,167
The LED costs about seven dollars and seventeen cents.

8
00:00:21,287 --> 00:00:25,278
That's about forty dollars and sixty-three cents a year, from one bulb.

9
00:00:25,398 --> 00:00:33,533
And in twenty twenty, about thirteen point six two million homes still left an incandescent or halogen bulb on outside all night.

10
00:00:33,653 --> 00:00:37,780
So if you change just one bulb, make it the one that's on while you sleep.

11
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,154
Like those two identical porch lights…
